[54.903278, "o", "\u001b[31m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[31m Error \u001b[0m\u001b[31m─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[31m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\u001b[31m \u001b[0m\u001b[39mUnknown option: \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m--image\u001b[0m\u001b[39m. Did you mean \u001b[0m\u001b[1;32m--tag\u001b[0m\u001b[39m?\u001b[0m\u001b[31m                                                                                                                \u001b[0m\u001b[31m \u001b[0m\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[55.014479, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@7148ca51-e916-4646-92df-6347040e0c56:/home/user/project# "]
[67.221364, "i", "prefect deploy --help\n"]
[67.221532, "o", "prefect deploy --help\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[68.081193, "o", "\u001b[1mUsage: \u001b[0m\u001b[1mprefect deploy COMMAND [OPTIONS]\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[68.081387, "o", "Create and manage deployments.\r\n\r\n"]
[68.084156, "o", "╭─ Commands ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\r\n│ \u001b[36minit\u001b[0m\u001b[36m  \u001b[0mInitialize a Prefect project.                                                                                                                          │\r\n╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\r\n"]
[68.090498, "o", "╭─ Session Parameters ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\r\n│ \u001b[36m--profile                                               \u001b[0m\u001b[36m  \u001b[0mSelect a profile for this CLI run.                                                                 │\r\n│ \u001b[36m--prompt --no-prompt                                    \u001b[0m\u001b[36m  \u001b[0mToggle interactive prompts.                                                                        │\r\n│ \u001b[36m--name -n --empty-name                                  \u001b[0m\u001b[36m  \u001b[0mThe name to give the deployment. Can be a pattern. Examples: 'my-deployment',                      │\r\n│ \u001b[36m                                                          \u001b[0m'my-flow/my-deployment', 'my-deployment-\u001b[3m', '\u001b[0m-flow-name/deployment*'                                │\r\n│ \u001b[36m--description -d                                        \u001b[0m\u001b[36m  \u001b[0mThe description to give the deployment. If not provided, the description will be populated from    │\r\n│ \u001b[36m                                                          \u001b[0mthe flow's description.                                                                            │\r\n│ \u001b[36m--version-type                                          \u001b[0m\u001b[36m  \u001b[0mThe type of version to use for this deployment.                                                    │\r\n│ \u001b[36m--version                                               \u001b[0m\u001b[36m  \u001b[0mA version to give the deployment.                                                                  │\r\n│ \u001b[36m--tag -t --empty-tag                                    \u001b[0m\u001b[36m  \u001b[0mOne or more optional tags to apply to the deployment. Note: tags are used only for organizational  │\r\n│ \u001b[36m                                                          \u001b[0mpurposes. For delegating work to workers, use the --work-queue flag.                               │\r\n│ \u001b[36m--concurrency-limit                                     \u001b[0m\u001b[36m  \u001b[0mThe maximum number of concurrent runs for this deployment.                                         │\r\n│ \u001b[36m--collision-strategy                                    \u001b[0m\u001b[36m  \u001b[0mConfigure the behavior for runs once the concurrency limit is reached. Falls back to \u001b[1;36;40mENQUEUE\u001b[0m if    │\r\n│ \u001b[36m                                                          \u001b[0munset.                                                                                             │\r\n│ \u001b[36m--pool -p                                               \u001b[0m\u001b[36m  \u001b[0mThe work pool that will handle this deployment's runs.                                             │\r\n│ \u001b[36m--work-queue -q                                         \u001b[0m\u001b[36m  \u001b[0mThe work queue that will handle this deployment's runs. It will be created if it doesn't already   │\r\n│ \u001b[36m                                                          \u001b[0mexist. Defaults to \u001b[1;36;40mNone\u001b[0m.                                                                           │\r\n│ \u001b[36m--job-variable --empty-job-variable                     \u001b[0m\u001b[36m  \u001b[0mOne or more job variable overrides for the work pool provided in the format of key=value string or │\r\n│ \u001b[36m                                                          \u001b[0ma JSON object                                                                                      │\r\n│ \u001b[36m--cron --empty-cron                                     \u001b[0m\u001b[36m  \u001b[0mA cron string that will be used to set a CronSchedule on the deployment.                           │\r\n│ \u001b[36m--interval --empty-interval                             \u001b[0m\u001b[36m  \u001b[0mAn integer specifying an interval (in seconds) that will be used to set an IntervalSchedule on the │\r\n│ \u001b[36m                                                          \u001b[0mdeployment.                                                                                        │\r\n│ \u001b[36m--anchor-date                                           \u001b[0m\u001b[36m  \u001b[0mThe anchor date for all interval schedules                                                         │\r\n│ \u001b[36m--rrule --empty-rrule                                   \u001b[0m\u001b[36m  \u001b[0mAn RRule that will be used to set an RRuleSchedule on the deployment.                              │\r\n│ \u001b[36m--timezone                                              \u001b[0m\u001b[36m  \u001b[0mDeployment schedule timezone string e.g. 'America/New_York'                                        │\r\n│ \u001b[36m--trigger --empty-trigger                               \u001b[0m\u001b[36m  \u001b[0mSpecifies a trigger for the deployment. The value can be a json string or path to \u001b[1;36;40m.yaml\u001b[0m/\u001b[1;36;40m.json\u001b[0m      │\r\n│ \u001b[36m                                                          \u001b[0mfile. This flag can be used multiple times.                                                        │\r\n│ \u001b[36m--param --empty-param                                   \u001b[0m\u001b[36m  \u001b[0mAn optional parameter override, values are parsed as JSON strings e.g. --param question=ultimate   │\r\n│ \u001b[36m                                                          \u001b[0m--param answer=42                                                                                  │\r\n│ \u001b[36m--params                                                \u001b[0m\u001b[36m  \u001b[0mAn optional parameter override in a JSON string format e.g. --params='{\"question\": \"ultimate\",     │\r\n│ \u001b[36m                                                          \u001b[0m\"answer\": 42}'                                                                                     │\r\n│ \u001b[36m--enforce-parameter-schema --no-enforce-parameter-schema\u001b[0m\u001b[36m  \u001b[0mWhether to enforce the parameter schema on this deployment. If set to True, any parameters passed  │\r\n│ \u001b[36m                                                          \u001b[0mto this deployment must match the signature of the flow. \u001b[2m[default: True]\u001b[0m                           │\r\n│ \u001b[36m--all --no-all                                          \u001b[0m\u001b[36m  \u001b[0mDeploy all flows in the project. If a flow name or entrypoint is also provided, this flag will be  │\r\n│ \u001b[36m                                                          \u001b[0mignored. \u001b[2m[default: False]\u001b[0m                                                                          │\r\n│ \u001b[36m--prefect-file                                          \u001b[0m\u001b[36m  \u001b[0mSpecify a custom path to a prefect.yaml file \u001b[2m[default: prefect.yaml]\u001b[0m                               │\r\n│ \u001b[36m--sla --empty-sla                                       \u001b[0m\u001b[36m  \u001b[0mExperimental: One or more SLA configurations for the deployment. May be removed or modified at any │\r\n│ \u001b[36m                                                          \u001b[0mtime. Currently only supported on Prefect Cloud.                                                   │\r\n╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\r\n"]
[68.214057, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@7148ca51-e916-4646-92df-6347040e0c56:/home/user/project# "]
